# PREIShare — TanStack Start (React 19, Vite 8, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, npm)

- App at repo root: routes in `src/routes/`, UI in `src/components/`, tokens in `src/styles.css`, router in `src/router.tsx`.
- File-based TanStack Router: export `Route` via `createFileRoute` / `createRootRoute`; default-export functional components.
- Imports: ESM (`"type": "module"`); path aliases `#/*` and `@/*` → `src/*`. Prefer `Link` for in-app nav.
- Style with Tailwind utilities plus CSS variables from `src/styles.css` (e.g. `--sea-ink`); keep the scaffold layout unless change is justified.
- Isomorphic by default: use `createServerFn` / `createServerOnlyFn` / `createClientOnlyFn` for env boundaries. Secrets via `process.env` on server only; client config only as `VITE_*`.
- Before Start/Router/Devtools edits: `npx @tanstack/intent@latest list` then `load` matching skills. Do not edit `src/routeTree.gen.ts` by hand.
- Always use TypeScript with strict mode.
- Follow existing component patterns in `src/components`.
- Use the Supabase client from `lib/supabase.ts`.
- Write tests for new features.

cat > .cursor/rules/preishare.mdc << 'EOF'
---
description: Project rules for PREIShare onboarding and agent behavior
alwaysApply: true
---

# PREIshare Rules

## Project identity
PREIshare (`preishare-org-repo`) is a single-package TypeScript web app.
It is not a monorepo — there is no `apps/` or `packages/` split.
Built from the TanStack CLI blank React Start scaffold.

## Stack (verified from package.json and AGENTS.md)
- TypeScript, React 19, TanStack Start / TanStack Router (file-based routes in `src/routes/`)
- Tailwind CSS v4, Vite 8
- Routes are generated via `tsr generate` — do not hand-edit generated route files
- No database, auth, or partner integrations exist in this app (confirmed blank scaffold)

## Preferred edit surfaces for newcomers
- `docs/onboarding/` — docs-only, low risk
- `README.md` — low risk
- `src/routes/`, `src/components/` — ask before editing until you understand the file-router convention
- Do not assume any file is safe just because it looks small

## Coding conventions (high-level)
- Import alias `#/*` maps to `./src/*`
- Prefer the smallest diff that solves the task — no drive-by refactors
- Do not invent scripts, packages, or folder names that aren't in `docs/onboarding/repo-map.md`
- No test script currently exists — do not assume test conventions that aren't there
- Load a matching Intent skill (`npx @tanstack/intent@latest list`) before Start/Router/Devtools changes

## Do-not rules (explicit)
- Never commit `.env` files or secret values, real or placeholder-that-looks-real
- Never hand-edit files produced by `tsr generate`
- Never delete or refactor a file without confirming nothing else imports it
- Never push directly to `upstream` — only to your own fork (`origin`)
- Ask before deleting any file

## Agent workflow
1. Plan the smallest change that satisfies the task
2. Ground every claim in `docs/onboarding/repo-map.md` — say "not found" instead of guessing
3. Make the diff
4. Verify (re-run relevant script, e.g. `npm run dev` or `npm run generate-routes`)
EOF